{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>From Asher — rich is his bread.</b> Since Asher supplied oil for the Temple — for meal-offerings and for all the other needs of the Temple — and it is known that all abundance and satiety come to the world from the Temple, therefore he said that from Asher is rich the bread of Israel, 'rich' in place of 'oil,' 'and he shall yield royal delicacies' — for he yields to the Temple and the Temple yields to all the world, like a king to the people. Or it is a prophecy that Asher will be a master of charity, and therefore all will praise him, sons and daughters, as it is written (Genesis 30:13) 'כִּי אִשְּׁרוּנִי בָנוֹת,' and Moses said (Deuteronomy 33:24) 'בָּרוּךְ מִבָּנִים אָשֵׁר' etc., and he gives to the poor rich bread and royal delicacies, not from the scantiest, like that one who fed the poor stuffed chickens (Ketuvot 67b), and as it is written (Job 31:17) 'אִם אָכַלְתִּי פִתִּי לְבַדִּי' — even my own special portion of fine bread, I did not eat alone."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:35.744095465Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}